# Agent Rules for agent_board

## Stdlib-Only Runtime Rule
The runtime must stay zero-dependency: `pyproject.toml [project] dependencies = []`.
Everything the board does (curses TUI, /proc scanning, JSON card files, ANSI
frames) uses the standard library only. Third-party tools are allowed as
*dev* dependencies (`[project.optional-dependencies].dev`) but must never
be imported at runtime.

## src/ Layout Rule
All implementation lives in `src/agent_board/` (`board.py`, `watch.py`).
The root-level `agent_board.py` is a launcher shim only: sys.path
bootstrap plus a `main()` call - never add features there. `agent-watch`
runs `src/agent_board/watch.py` directly via the `~/sbin/agent-watch`
symlink.
The root file `agent_board` (no extension) is the bash service manager;
shell logic goes there, not into the Python package. (The wrapper file
blocks a root-level package directory, which is why the package lives
under `src/`.)

## Proper and Complete pyproject.toml Rule
`pyproject.toml` must stay PEP 517/518/621-compliant and complete:
`[build-system]` (setuptools), full `[project]` metadata, `[project.scripts]`
for every CLI entry, `[tool.ruff]`, `[tool.mypy]`, and
`[tool.pytest.ini_options]`. `[project.urls]` is added when the repository
gets a public remote - do not invent placeholder URLs. No legacy
`setup.py`-only packaging.

## Version Stamp Rule
Versions are `Major.Minor.<14-digit UTC timestamp>Z` (trailing `Z`).
Bump the stamp on every material change, before the commit:
- `pyproject.toml [project] version` carries the same 14-digit timestamp
  WITHOUT the Z (PEP 440 forbids the Z); `src/agent_board/board.py
  __version__` keeps the Z; the two must match modulo the Z
  (`./_check_version` enforces this).
- `src/agent_board/watch.py __version__` carries its own Major.Minor with
  the same timestamp.
- Every helper script carries its own `__VERSION__` stamp, bumped when
  that script changes.

## Commit Before Changes
Before implementing a new step or changing any module, commit the current
state with the current version (`./_git` or
`git commit -m "<stamp>: <summary>"`). Never mix unrelated changes into
one commit.

## Tests Before Commit
`./_tests` must pass before every commit. The installed `hooks/pre-commit`
enforces pytest (quick mode), `ruff check src tests`,
`mypy src/agent_board`, and `./_check_version`; bypass single modules only
deliberately (`SKIP_TESTS=1`) and never silently.

## History Rule
1. `history.md` (repo root) is the release log: newest entry on top, one
   entry per version bump, written before the release commit; the latest
   entry doubles as the release notes.
2. `history/` is the working archive: `prompts/`, `changes/`, `todo/`,
   `plans/`, `tests/`, `ideas/`, `goals/` - archive with a unified
   `YYYYMMDDThhmmss` timestamp in the filename; never delete archived files.
3. Decisions get their own dated entry in `history.md`, including reasoning
   and rejected alternatives (see the 2026-09-13 textual decision).

## Docstring Style
`docstrings-python` (`~/.agents/skills/docstrings-python/skill.md`) governs
every Python function: PEP 257 summary in the imperative mood ending with a
period, Google-style `Args:`/`Returns:`/`Raises:` sections, `Attributes:` on
classes. Types live in the signature, never in the docstring prose. Enforce it
on new and changed functions and strip the retired `python_comment_style`
header (`usage:`/`returns:`/`errors:`) whenever you touch such a function.
Check with `ruff check --select D` (configured in `pyproject.toml`).

## Line Endings
LF everywhere; `.gitattributes` enforces `* text=auto eol=lf`. Never write
CRLF files into this repository.

## Dash Rule
Never use the em dash character (U+2014) in any text: markdown files,
docstrings, help texts, UI strings, commit messages, chat replies. Use a
plain hyphen `-` instead. Box-drawing characters (U+2500 table rules in
the board frames and comments) are not dashes and stay untouched.